From f49e0ab12bbae7106a407e62667ac2b69e8a62a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cgscli <cgscli@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:53:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] P16: update from the cgs package on npm

Reason: A CGS build must update from its own release, never from omp's channels (they would replace it with upstream omp). The source, the installer and the verification are inside update-cli and the startup check, which the extension API cannot reach.
Upstream: none (distribution-specific update source)
Remove-when: CGS stops shipping a branded omp build

- cli/cgs-release.ts: reads the `latest` document of the npm package `@cicori/cgs` from the npm registry and npmmirror at once, first answer wins (CGS_REGISTRY_URL replaces the list) and validates it
- `cgs update` and `--check`: compare with the running version, install the release tarball with `bun install -g --registry=<answering registry>`, verify through the `cgs` launcher
- startup check and auto-update offer only that release; the notice says `cgs update`
- replaces the P4 gate that disabled updating unless PI_BUILD_URL was set
- the recovery hint of a failed verification is `bun install -g @cicori/cgs`: omp's own installer (omp.sh) would put upstream omp on the PATH
